==============================================================================
s_recur  M1 : can a polynomial operator kill the zeta_2(5) coefficient
             of the M=6 rank-2 family and keep the zeta_2(7) one?
==============================================================================

[R0] CONTROL -- the operator search on a family where the answer is known:
     M=4, m=1 (LSZ) has rank 1 already; rho_3 is the only coefficient.
     A kernel for rho_3 must therefore also kill rho_0 (S == 0).

[R1] single symmetric form, shifts only (the minimal recurrence route)
      built 79 rho-vectors up to n=84 in 3s
      unknowns C=55, equations=75, rank=55 -> dim ker(rho_3) = 0
      of the 0 kernel vectors, 0 give a NON-zero rho_5

[R2] wider operator: L=6, D=12
      built 117 rho-vectors up to n=122 in 10s
      unknowns C=91, equations=111, rank=91 -> dim ker(rho_3) = 0
      of the 0 kernel vectors, 0 give a NON-zero rho_5

[R3] the inset cone: 4 distinct forms, shifts L=3, D=8
      built 668 rho-vectors up to n=172 in 108s
      unknowns C=144, equations=164, rank=78 -> dim ker(rho_3) = 66
      of the 66 kernel vectors, 0 give a NON-zero rho_5
